# Shell scripts copied into the Docker image must stay LF — a CRLF shebang
# (#!/bin/sh\r) breaks the container entrypoint when built from a Windows checkout.
docker/*.sh text eol=lf

# Skill bundles are MATERIALIZED into every worktree by the board (agent-skill-files.ts),
# which writes LF. Without this, git normalizes the checked-out copy to CRLF on Windows and
# the freshly-materialized file reads as modified with an EMPTY diff — so every worktree the
# board touches is permanently dirty. That is not cosmetic: `workspaceLaunchPreflight`
# refuses to relaunch when the worktree "has uncommitted changes", so a workspace that lands
# in `error` for any unrelated reason can never be recovered through the API, and the error's
# own advice ("commit the workspace first") would commit pure line-ending churn into the
# ticket's branch. Pinning LF makes materialization a no-op in git's eyes. (#217)
.claude/skills/** text eol=lf

# A file that vitest TRANSFORMS must be LF if it carries a shebang. `scripts/*.mjs` are
# imported directly by tests (dev-script.test.mjs imports ten of them), and under CRLF the
# `#!/usr/bin/env node` line survives the transform's shebang strip — the `#!` then sits
# inside the wrapped module, which dies with `SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token` and
# is reported as `no tests`.
#
# This bit ONLY outside the main checkout, which is why it went unexplained for so long: main
# happened to hold `scripts/ensure-shared-fresh.mjs` as LF, while every fresh clone and every
# board worktree gets CRLF from core.autocrlf=true. dev-script.test.mjs is @gate:always-run,
# so the pre-merge gate failed on EVERY branch and no merge could land at all. Proven by
# bisection: that one file, CRLF, is sufficient; the same file CRLF minus its shebang passes.
# (#703 — see shebang-eol-guard.test.ts, which stops the class from recurring.)
scripts/** text eol=lf

# The rest of the repo's shebang files, same reason as `scripts/**` above. This is a
# deliberately NARROW pin rather than a repo-wide `* text=auto eol=lf`: the main checkout is
# genuinely mixed (measured at 1234 LF vs 1855 CRLF files), so a global flip would rewrite
# ~1855 files on disk for every checkout — a large, unrelated change to carry on a fix for a
# merge outage. Pinning the files that actually carry `#!` is necessary and sufficient, and
# `shebang-eol-guard.test.ts` fails on a NEW shebang file that is not covered here, so the
# list cannot silently fall behind. (#703)
# Directory-level pins for the two tooling trees, matching the .claude/skills/** rule above.
.claude/hooks/** text eol=lf
.codex/skills/** text eol=lf
packages/desktop/src-tauri/src/main.rs text eol=lf
packages/mcp-server/src/index.ts text eol=lf
packages/server/bin/*.js text eol=lf
# Bundled plugins. `**` on BOTH sides: a plugin's `tools/` tree nests (jira-sync has
# `tools/sync/*.mjs`), which a single-`*` tail would miss. There is deliberately no
# repo-root `plugins/**` rule any more — a bundled plugin lives here or it is not bundled
# (see docs/plugin-development.md, "Bundling a plugin with the board").
packages/server/plugins/**/tools/**/*.mjs text eol=lf
packages/server/scripts/*.mjs text eol=lf
packages/server/src/cli/index.ts text eol=lf
packages/server/src/scaffold/*.js text eol=lf
packages/server/src/scaffold/*.mjs text eol=lf
packages/server/src/worker/worker-cli.ts text eol=lf

# The OpenAPI spec is GENERATED (scripts/generate-openapi.ts writes LF) and then asserted on
# by tests that match a path key together with its exact line terminator. With core.autocrlf=true git checked it
# out as CRLF into every worktree while the main checkout kept the generator's LF bytes, so
# openapi-thrown-status.test.ts passed on master and failed in ALL twelve worktrees — i.e. in
# every pre-merge gate run, for every branch, which is what stalled the merge queue. Pinning
# LF makes the checked-out bytes the generated bytes everywhere. (#885)
packages/server/openapi.yaml text eol=lf

# NOTE — there is deliberately NO `docs/tests/impact-map.json merge=ours` line here any more.
#
# #952 committed the test-impact map and needed a `merge=ours` driver so a branch carrying an
# older copy could not stall a merge on a 1.4 MB one-line-per-entry JSON conflict. That whole
# mechanism was load-bearing only because the file was tracked, and it never worked on its own:
# git has no built-in `ours` driver, so the attribute had to be paired with a `.git/config`
# registration the board performed on every pass.
#
# #1018 made the map an UNTRACKED, gitignored artifact (see `.gitignore`), because the
# `chore: rebuild test-impact map` commits it required were moving the base tip under running
# pre-merge gates. An untracked file cannot conflict, so the attribute, the driver registration
# and the divergent-merge test that pinned them are all gone together. Do not re-add this line
# without first re-tracking the map — an attribute for a path git never merges is dead config
# that a later reader will take as documentation.
